+# Pull-to-refresh + freshness Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: superpowers:subagent-driven-development. Steps use checkbox syntax.
+
+**Goal:** Pull down on Teraz/Miejsca to re-fetch live GIOŚ data (refetching the active place + all rows via one global signal), and show the data's age on Miejsca rows.
+
+**Architecture:** A `RefreshProvider` holds a `signal` (bumped on pull) + a `refreshing` boolean (tied to the active place's refetch settle + an 8s safety timeout). `usePlaceReading`/`usePlaceDetail` add the signal to their effect deps (a bump refetches). `useRefreshSignal()` returns `0` when no provider is mounted, so the existing hook/screen suites need no changes. `RefreshControl` on both screens.
+
+**Tech Stack:** TS strict, RN 0.86, Jest + @testing-library/react-native (render/renderHook ASYNC — await). No new dependency (`RefreshControl` is on board).
+
+## Global Constraints
+- No new dependency. · TS strict, no `any`. · `src/core` pure, 100% coverage. · files ≤200 / functions ≤40. · imports one-way (features→shared→core; features never import data). · behavior tests cite AC IDs.
+- Spec `docs/specs/018-refresh.md` is authoritative. Model: active-place-tied `refreshing` + 8s timeout + debounce; NO in-flight counter. `useRefreshSignal()` defaults to `0` unwrapped.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: `shared/refresh` — RefreshProvider + hooks
+
+**Files:**
+- Create: `src/shared/refresh/index.tsx`
+- Test: `src/shared/refresh/__tests__/RefreshProvider.test.tsx`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `RefreshProvider({children})`; `useRefreshSignal(): number` (0 when unwrapped); `useRefresh(): { refresh(): void; refreshing: boolean; settleActive(): void }`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing test (AC-1)** — with fake timers (`jest.useFakeTimers()`):
+  - `refresh()` increments the value returned by `useRefreshSignal()` by 1 and flips `refreshing` true.
+  - `settleActive()` sets `refreshing` false and cancels the timeout.
+  - if `settleActive` never comes, advancing 8s (`jest.advanceTimersByTime(8000)`) flips `refreshing` false (safety).
+  - a second `refresh()` while `refreshing` is a no-op (signal unchanged — debounce).
+  - `useRefreshSignal()` / `useRefresh()` used with NO `RefreshProvider` → signal `0`, `refresh`/`settleActive` are safe no-ops (render a component using them outside the provider; no throw).
+
+  Drive it via a tiny harness component that renders `useRefreshSignal()` + buttons calling `useRefresh()` actions (use `fireEvent.press` + `screen.getByText` for the current signal), awaiting the async `render`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run, verify fail** — `npx jest src/shared/refresh`.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** `src/shared/refresh/index.tsx`:
+
+```tsx
+import {
+  createContext, useCallback, useContext, useMemo, useRef, useState,
+  type ReactNode,
+} from 'react';
+
+const SAFETY_MS = 8000;
+
+type RefreshApi = { refresh: () => void; refreshing: boolean; settleActive: () => void };
+const SignalCtx = createContext<number>(0);
+const ApiCtx = createContext<RefreshApi>({
+  refresh: () => {}, refreshing: false, settleActive: () => {},
+});
+
+export function RefreshProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
+  const [signal, setSignal] = useState(0);
+  const [refreshing, setRefreshing] = useState(false);
+  const timer = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);
+  const refreshingRef = useRef(false);
+
+  const clear = useCallback(() => {
+    if (timer.current) {
+      clearTimeout(timer.current);
+      timer.current = null;
+    }
+    refreshingRef.current = false;
+    setRefreshing(false);
+  }, []);
+
+  const refresh = useCallback(() => {
+    if (refreshingRef.current) return; // debounce while refreshing
+    refreshingRef.current = true;
+    setRefreshing(true);
+    setSignal(s => s + 1);
+    timer.current = setTimeout(clear, SAFETY_MS); // safety: never stick
+  }, [clear]);
+
+  const settleActive = useCallback(() => {
+    if (refreshingRef.current) clear();
+  }, [clear]);
+
+  const api = useMemo<RefreshApi>(
+    () => ({ refresh, refreshing, settleActive }),
+    [refresh, refreshing, settleActive],
+  );
+  return (
+    <SignalCtx.Provider value={signal}>
+      <ApiCtx.Provider value={api}>{children}</ApiCtx.Provider>
+    </SignalCtx.Provider>
+  );
+}
+
+export function useRefreshSignal(): number {
+  return useContext(SignalCtx);
+}
+export function useRefresh(): RefreshApi {
+  return useContext(ApiCtx);
+}
+```
+(Contexts have safe defaults → unwrapped usage never throws and `signal` is `0`.)
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests** — green.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Full gate** — `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` green, `src/core` 100%. Commit: `feat(refresh): RefreshProvider — global signal + refreshing lifecycle (AC-1)`.
+
+---
+
+### Task 2: Wire the signal into the fetch hooks + ActivePlace settle + App
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/shared/place/usePlaceReading.ts`, `src/shared/place/usePlaceDetail.ts`
+- Modify: `src/shared/place/ActivePlaceContext.tsx`
+- Modify: `App.tsx`
+- Test: extend `src/shared/place/__tests__/usePlaceReading.test.tsx` (+ usePlaceDetail) and add a small integration test for AC-3/AC-3b.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `useRefreshSignal`, `useRefresh` (Task 1).
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests (AC-2, AC-3, AC-3b)**
+  - AC-2: render `usePlaceReading(place)` inside `RefreshProvider` with a fake `AirQualitySource` counting `getCurrentReading`: 1 call on mount; after `refresh()` = 2; an unrelated re-render (signal unchanged) = still 2. Same for `usePlaceDetail`/`getDetail`. Then render WITHOUT `RefreshProvider` → still 1 call, no throw (unwrapped-0 guards the existing suites).
+  - AC-3/AC-3b: render `ActivePlaceProvider` inside `RefreshProvider` with a fake source; `useRefresh().refreshing` is false during initial load; after `refresh()` it's true; once the active reading re-settles (fake resolves) it flips false.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run, verify fail**.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement**
+  - `usePlaceReading.ts`: add `const signal = useRefreshSignal();` and include `signal` in the effect deps array `[sourceForPlace, placeKey, signal]`. Keep the existing `eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` (still excludes only the `place` object). Same edit in `usePlaceDetail.ts`.
+  - `ActivePlaceContext.tsx`: `const { settleActive } = useRefresh();` and add an effect keyed on the reading `state` that calls `settleActive()` (clears `refreshing` when the active place's refetch settles; harmless no-op when not refreshing). Add `settleActive` to that effect's deps (it's stable).
+  - `App.tsx`: wrap the provider tree in `<RefreshProvider>` ABOVE `PlaceSourceProvider` and `ActivePlaceProvider` (so the active place + all rows share one signal).
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests** — `npm test` green (existing place suites must stay green — the unwrapped-0 default guarantees no behavior change without a provider).
+- [ ] **Step 5: Full gate** green. Commit: `feat(refresh): fetch hooks refetch on signal; ActivePlace clears refreshing (AC-2, AC-3)`.
+
+---
+
+### Task 3: RefreshControl on Teraz + Miejsca
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/features/teraz/TerazScreen.tsx`, `src/features/miejsca/MiejscaScreen.tsx`
+- Test: extend their tests to assert a `RefreshControl` is wired to `refresh`/`refreshing`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `useRefresh` (Task 1).
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing test** — render each screen inside `RefreshProvider` (+ the providers they need); assert the `ScrollView` has a `refreshControl` prop whose `onRefresh` is the `refresh` fn (query by testID on the RefreshControl, or assert the ScrollView receives `refreshing`). Keep it a behavior check (not a snapshot).
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run, verify fail**.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** — in each screen: `const { refresh, refreshing } = useRefresh();` and pass to the `ScrollView`:
+  ```tsx
+  refreshControl={
+    <RefreshControl refreshing={refreshing} onRefresh={refresh} tintColor={colors.text.dim} testID="refresh-control" />
+  }
+  ```
+  (import `RefreshControl` from `react-native`; use a dark-theme `tintColor` from tokens). Confirm both screens are `ScrollView` (MiejscaScreen is — spec).
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests** — green.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Full gate** green. Commit: `feat(refresh): pull-to-refresh control on Teraz + Miejsca`.
+
+---
+
+### Task 4: Miejsca row data-age
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/features/miejsca/PlaceRow.tsx`
+- Test: extend `src/features/miejsca/__tests__/PlaceRow.test.tsx`
+
+**Interfaces:**
